>> title: Potato Knish
>> category: Dumplings & Rolls
>> tags: potato, onion, baked, pastry, deli
>> counters: Deli
>> aka: knish, knishes, square knish, potato knish, baked knish, knysh
>> pairs-with: schmaltz, sour-dill-pickles, chicken-broth
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr 15 min
>> slack: forgiving — the mash has no room in it: a potato mashed smooth goes gluey, and a gluey knish is heavy all the way through
>> step.1: mix the dough, rest 1 hr
>> step.2: boil the potatoes 20 min
>> step.3: fry the onions 20 min in schmaltz
>> step.4: mash coarse, season hard
>> step.5: roll thin, fill the sheet, lay the top
>> step.6: brush with egg, bake 45 min, cut into squares

Mix @all-purpose flour{2%cups}(250 g), @baking powder{1%tsp} and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} with @egg{1%large}, @neutral oil{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @warm water{1/2%cup}(120 mL) and @white vinegar{1%tsp} into a soft, slightly sticky dough, knead it for a minute, then oil it, cover it and ~rest{1%hr}.

Boil @russet potatoes{2%lb}(900 g, peeled, in chunks) in @water{3%qt} with @kosher salt{1%Tbs} and ~boil{20%min}, until they fall off a knife, then drain them dry in the hot pan for a minute.

Fry @yellow onions{2%large}(diced) in @schmaltz{1/4%cup}(60 mL) over medium heat and ~fry{20%min}, until deep gold.

Mash @&(~2)drained potatoes{} coarse with @&(~1)fried onions{} and all the fat in their pan, @kosher salt{2%tsp} and @black pepper{1%tsp}.

Roll @&(~4)rested dough{} on a floured cloth until you can nearly see through it, line a #sheet pan{}, spread @&(~1)potato filling{} an inch thick, and fold the overhang over to seal.

Brush @&(~1)filled sheet{} with @egg{1%large}(beaten with a splash of water) and ~bake{45%min} at 400°F (200°C), until the top is glossy and deep brown, then cut it into eight squares while it is still warm.
